0. How to use this document
1. Save as /docs/SPEC.md in the repo root.
2. Paste Section 16 into Claude Code or Cursor. It tells the agent this file is authoritative.
3. Reliability promise. No system is literally unbreakable. This design guarantees: (a) an invalid plan is never persisted or shown, (b) committed data is never lost, (c) every dependency failure degrades to a reduced working mode, never a blank error page.
1. Product Requirements (PRD)
1.1 Problem
Event planning fails at change, not at creation. A venue falls through, guests go from 80 to 150, the budget is cut, and every spreadsheet, WhatsApp thread and checklist is stale within a day. Existing GenAI planners emit a one-time checklist and go silent.
1.2 Solution
Aayojan maintains one verified, versioned Event object (budget, timeline, vendors, tasks, ideas) and re-solves it after every change. An LLM translates language into typed operations; deterministic code applies, validates, scores and diffs them. The user always sees what changed and why.
1.3 Personas
• Riya, 28: plans her sister's 200-guest Jaipur wedding on a Rs 12L budget; needs a plan she can trust and share with family.
• Arjun, 34: plans a 10-year-old's birthday; wants ideas and a fast, cheap plan.
• Meena, 52: RWA secretary running a community Diwali mela; needs permits, volunteers, sponsors, donations.
• Collaborators: family, vendors, volunteers; read-limited role views via share link.
1.4 Goals and non-goals
Goals: living plan, explainable replan, measurable validity, three event modes, premium UX, shareable and exportable output. Non-goals (v1): payments, vendor marketplace, native mobile apps, real vendor bookings, multi-language UI (Hinglish drafts only).
