2. Core concept and invariants
The Event is one JSON document, versioned. Every mutation produces a new immutable version. Invariants, enforced by the validator before any write:
• I1 Budget lines sum exactly to total budget (integer rupees).
• I2 Contingency >= 5% of budget.
• I3 Every open task due date lies between today and the event date (completed tasks exempt from the past-date rule).
• I4 Every dependency id exists and the graph is acyclic.
• I5 A dependency never finishes after its dependent starts.
• I6 Locked budget lines are never changed by automatic rebalancing.
• I7 Venue capacity >= guest count where the venue declares capacity.
• I8 Every task category exists in the event-type template.
• I9 Version number increases by exactly 1 and the parent version exists.
• I10 All text fields are length-bounded and sanitized.
If an operation set violates an invariant it is rejected with machine-readable reason codes. The LLM retries with those codes (max 2). If it still fails, the user sees a plain-language explanation and the plan stays unchanged. The LLM never grades itself.
