Key decisions:
1. LLM proposes typed operations; code disposes. The model never writes the Event directly. It returns a list of ops from a closed vocabulary and the Domain Engine applies them. This removes whole classes of corruption.
2. Pure domain core. The engine has no IO, so it is property-testable and runs identically in preview and commit.
3. Immutable versions. Undo, diff, audit and realtime sync all come from the version table.
4. Two paths. Deterministic fast path (sliders, form edits, under 1s) and LLM path (language edits, generation, drafts).
5. Jobs for anything over 2s, streamed over SSE with stage events; the client can reconnect and resume by job id.
