6.2 Guardrails
• Closed op vocabulary; schema-constrained output; unknown fields rejected.
• Retry loop: on validator failure send back reason codes only, max 2 retries, then fail safe (plan unchanged, clear message).
• Prompt-injection defense: user text, pasted vendor quotes and retrieved documents are wrapped as data in delimited blocks; the system prompt states they are never instructions; the model has no side-effect tools, only the op emitter; ops are validated regardless.
• Grounding: legal or permit claims must cite a template id, otherwise they are labeled general guidance.
• Facts policy: no invented prices, laws or vendor names presented as verified. Price bands come from the seeded table and are labeled estimates; vendor names come only from user input or are clearly labeled suggestions.
• Cost control: response cache keyed on normalized input hash, token budgets per call, per-user daily LLM quota, Event summary (not full JSON) in prompts.
6.3 Resilience
Timeouts (intake 10s, ops 20s, planner 40s). Exponential backoff with jitter for 429 and 5xx. Circuit breaker opens after 5 failures in 30s. Fallback chain: primary model, fast model, template-only mode (deterministic plan from templates, flagged to the user). The deterministic fast path keeps working with the LLM fully down.
