8. Realtime design
• Job progress: SSE with heartbeat every 15s, event ids for resume, automatic fallback to polling after two failed reconnects.
• Multi-user sync: Supabase Realtime channel event:{id} broadcasts version_committed (version, diff summary). Clients apply the diff or refetch; stale local edits get a 409 and a merge prompt only when the same entity changed.
• Presence: avatars and who is viewing which tab; ephemeral, never persisted.
• Optimistic UI: sliders render from the local TypeScript engine and reconcile to the server preview.
• Offline: read-only cached plan via service worker; queued task-status edits replay on reconnect with idempotency keys.
• Shared test vectors: one JSON file of input/expected-output pairs runs against both the Python and TypeScript engines in CI, so preview and commit can never disagree.
