9.3 States and quality bars
Every screen defines empty, loading (skeleton, never spinner-only), partial, error (plain language, retry, what is preserved), offline, and degraded (banner: 'Smart suggestions are limited right now; your plan is safe'). LLM-driven changes show ops as chips before applying. Copy is warm, short, specific. Accessibility: visible focus rings, ARIA live regions for streamed updates, color never the sole signal, 44px touch targets, contrast >= 4.5:1. Lighthouse mobile targets: performance >= 90, accessibility >= 95.
10. Security and privacy
• Auth: Supabase Auth (email OTP, Google). JWT verified in FastAPI via cached JWKS; short expiry.
• Authorization: owner checks in code plus Postgres RLS (defense in depth). Share tokens: 256-bit random, stored as peppered SHA-256 hash, shown once, scoped, expiring, revocable, rate-limited.
• Input: Pydantic strict validation; length caps (brief 4,000 chars, instruction 1,000); output escaped on render; no raw HTML from the model; markdown sanitized.
• Secrets: platform secret stores only; gitleaks in CI; rotation runbook.
• Transport: HTTPS only, HSTS, strict CSP, CORS allowlist, SameSite cookies.
• Abuse: per-user LLM quotas, global spend cap with automatic switch to template-only mode, Turnstile on anonymous trials.
• Privacy: collect minimum PII; redaction middleware keeps PII out of logs; export and delete endpoints; provider-side training use disabled; plain privacy note in the UI.
• Supply chain: pinned lockfiles, Dependabot, pip-audit and npm audit in CI.
11. Reliability and production hardening
Risk
Mitigation
LLM down or slow
timeouts, jittered retries, circuit breaker, fallback model, template-only mode; deterministic fast path unaffected
Invalid LLM output
schema + closed ops + validator + 2 retries + fail-safe unchanged plan
Concurrent edits
optimistic locking (409), versioned writes, merge prompt
Duplicate requests
Idempotency-Key table; jobs unique on key
Worker crash mid-job
per-stage persisted status; jobs running over 120s are reaped and retried once
DB failure
managed Postgres, PITR backups (daily + WAL), pgbouncer pooling, expand-then-contract migrations
Redis failure
rate limiting falls back to in-memory limiter; jobs fall back to in-process queue with a warning
Traffic spike
horizontal replicas, autoscale on CPU and queue depth, per-user quotas, request size limits, CDN for static and share views
Bad deploy
CI gates, preview deploys, 10% canary, automatic rollback on error-rate breach, feature flags
Export failure
exports built from an immutable version snapshot; PDF timeout with retry; async if over 5s
Date bugs
ISO dates in Asia/Kolkata, no naive datetimes, property tests across leap years and month ends
