12. Testing and evaluation
• Unit and property-based (Hypothesis): for any sequence of random valid ops the engine output passes the validator or is rejected with a reason; budget always sums; rescale is idempotent; no cycles; dates ordered. 10,000 cases per property in CI.
• Cross-language vectors: Python and TypeScript engines agree on 500 vectors.
• Golden evals (50 scripted edits): guests up and down, budget cuts and raises, venue cancelled, date earlier and later, type switch, locked lines, infeasible budgets, injection attempts embedded in text, ambiguous instructions, Hinglish input. Metrics: first-pass validity, validity after retry, diff precision (no unrelated changes), median latency, cost. Published at /status and in the README.
• Adversarial: prompt-injection corpus, oversized input, unicode edge cases.
• E2E (Playwright): full demo script at desktop and 360px; offline and reconnect; two-browser realtime sync.
• Load (k6): 200 concurrent users on non-LLM endpoints with p95 <= 300ms; 50 concurrent LLM jobs against a mocked provider.
• Chaos: LLM returns 500s, Redis killed, worker killed mid-job, slow DB; assert the degraded behaviors in Section 11.
• Accessibility: axe in CI plus a manual keyboard pass.
Definition of done for any feature: unit tests, an eval case if LLM-touching, defined empty and error states, telemetry, docs updated.
